{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118483","id":3519283865,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7RxAKZ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118483","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118483.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118483.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118483","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118483/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118483/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118483/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6c1306773ceeaa4445d129b98851b2004cb8a89b","number":118483,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix `ERR_PRINT` usage in forked child process lead to possible crashing","user":{"login":"TsFreddie","id":3797859,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3OTc4NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3797859?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie","html_url":"https://github.com/TsFreddie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TsFreddie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"closes: #118189 \r\n\r\npossibly related: #114393 #111813 #116983 #114547 #73965\r\n\r\n## Investigation\r\n\r\nIn #118189 I said that deleting a file crashes godot-mono build on my machine. I managed to caught the crash site in a debugger on my machine, but they are almost always in C#'s JIT compiler in coreclr.\r\n\r\nIn my issue I also said I managed to find a way to not crash it if I built it, but later on I found out it didn't crash when I run it in my vscode terminal. Turns out my vscode package bundled `gio`.\r\n\r\nSo I started investigating the seemingly unharmful log \"Could not create child process: gio\". Found this `ERR_PRINT` call in a fork.\r\n\r\n## Possible problems\r\n\r\nI'm not 100% sure this is the case, but this did fix my crash on my machine. I couldn't dig any further into C# runtime or anything `ERR_PRINT` touches, but I have a rough feeling about the following things `ERR_PRINT` accesses:\r\n\r\n* `OS::get_singleton()->print_error()`\r\n  * This singleton is a frozen copy from the parent. It's probably fine, but I just have bad feeling about it.\r\n* `ScriptServer::capture_script_backtraces()`\r\n  * This is probably what crashed my editor on my machine, when it eventually want to capture C#'s stack trace, reaching `DebuggingUtils.GetCurrentStackInfo()` which does a `new StackTrace()`.\r\n  * Without digging into .NET too much, I assume it accessed the heap from another process which leads to the eventual corruption of my C# runtime and crashes.\r\n* `_global_lock()`\r\n  * The lock is a copied over mutex. Just bad vibes.\r\n* `error_handler_list`\r\n  * Copied over handlers, if anything in it does anything cross process it's probably bad.\r\n\r\nAnyway, doing anything other than `exec` after a `fork` feels bad.\r\n\r\n## Alternative solutions\r\n\r\nThis fix moves the error messages out of the editor console and doesn't have pretty print or stack trace. If it has to have it, other solutions might be:\r\n\r\n* A fork-friendly print function\r\n* Some way to signal error back to parent process and print\r\n* Give up `fork()` in favor of other way of spawning\r\n\r\n## Pertinent\r\n\r\nI also realized, there is almost no way on unix system for `create_process` caller to know the command didn't spawn and immediately quit since these methods always returns the pid of the fork.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://ap